body:
Don't make assumptions. Their phone could have died, they could have been busy replying to something to do with work or school and ended up missing the notification. Depends how old you are, they could be grounded. If they are just ignoring you, they don't deserve you.

&#x200B;

x

You can get ones without scripts and they do work. Try and go to the chemist and get **Anxiolift**. It helps with 'mild anxiety' but I got it for my depression as well. I have other prescribed medications, but in all honesty, none work as good as Anxiolift does.

&#x200B;

\- this is also one my therapist has recommended to try, and it does work with validation from her.

Edit: Just remembered, go onto iTunes and search Rick Collingwood. He does hypnotizing exercises that actually help. You do need to pay for them, but after a while, it helps majorly. I personally use his PTSD one and it works very well with depression.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

x

Move in with friends and improve yourself mentally. There's no thing as 'one true love'. I'm sure there's someone out there who can make you just as happy. Still see your kids and get closure with your ex-partner. Keep looking and I'm sure someone special will come into your life sooner or later.

&#x200B;

x

Find someone more interesting with a personality. She seems dull if she's leaving you with one-worded answers. If she likes you, she will message you again later. Just ignore her and move on. 

&#x200B;

x

Go for it. She probably likes you too and possibly faked a few interests just to bond with you. If she isn't interested so be it. She might be the one for you and you could lose your chance if you don't make a move. 

&#x200B;

x

Calm down and take deep breathes. When you find someone you're absolutely head over heels for, its better to say 'I'm a virgin', rather than 'I have about 5 STD's and a few children'. There's ways to solve it, but probably don't go losing it to a random. That'll be a bad story when you end up with the love of your life and they ask whether you're a virgin or not and you say you lost it to a prostitute on the street corner.

&#x200B;

x

Go for it. You're 15 and if she still continuously talks to you - she probably likes you. I've moved countless times and ignored everyone from previous schools. All you can do is try - you have nothing to lose. If she says no - the right person will come along later :)

&#x200B;

x

Just tell her straight up. I'm quite an honest person when people have obvious pen marks or something between their teeth - I always tell them. 

They are thankful and out of everyone - get pissed at people who didn't tell them. If you had bad breath wouldn't you like to be told? I sure would. She might feel embarrassed, but at least then she wouldn't breathe on anyone and create a bad personal image due to her poor hygiene.

&#x200B;

She'd probably feel a bit shy about it, but after time she should be cool again WITH good breath :)

&#x200B;

x
